+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive coffee homepage with browser-encrypted delivery notes.
+
+Install dependencies with `pnpm install` and produce the static site with `pnpm run build`. Deploy the generated `dist/` directory over HTTPS. `pnpm start` is the development command; it is not required for a production build.
+
+## Delivery notes
+
+This is a **local session preview**, since this project has no delivery backend. No note or key is sent anywhere. A save generates a fresh recipient key pair in the tab, encapsulates to its public key, and encrypts the note. Only the ciphertext envelope and recipient key remain in application memory; the editor is cleared. Refresh, navigation away, or deletion clears the session. No notes or keys are written to local storage, cookies, analytics, or console logs.
+
+- Default hybrid mode: noble's X-Wing (`ml_kem768_x25519`), combining ML-KEM-768 and X25519.
+- Post-quantum mode: ML-KEM-768.
+- Both modes: HKDF-SHA-256 with a fresh 32-byte salt and application/suite/recipient context derives a non-exportable AES-256-GCM key. Every save has a fresh random 12-byte nonce and a 128-bit authentication tag.
+- Version, purpose, suite, recipient key ID, timestamp, encapsulation, salt, and nonce are authenticated as additional data. Tampering causes reveal to fail.
+- Reveal uses recipient-side decapsulation, then authenticated decryption. Revealed text uses `textContent` and hides after 30 seconds or when the document is hidden.
+- Delete overwrites the recipient secret-key byte array and releases the envelope. JavaScript strings and garbage-collected memory cannot be guaranteed to be securely erased.
+- Download exports only the encrypted envelope. **There is intentionally no private-key export or persistent recovery; downloaded copies cannot be decrypted after this session ends.**
+
+For actual delivery, replace the local recipient with a provisioned, authenticated public key from the delivery service, send only the encrypted envelope to an authenticated API, and keep the recipient private key outside the customer client. Recipient key rotation, authorization, retention, and staff-side decryption need a backend integration. The homepage does not claim to implement these services. Browser encryption requires HTTPS or localhost and does not protect against compromised scripts or devices.
+
+Cryptographic implementation reference: https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum
